<newsitem itemid="65592" id="root" date="1996-09-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Clinton Cards cuts H1 losses.</title>
<headline>Clinton Cards cuts H1 losses.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to Aug 4</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		8.15 loss	    vs 10.68 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.85		   vs 1.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.3 loss	     vs 2.8 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   67.3		   vs 50.8</p>
<p> Operating result	 2.4 loss	     vs 2.9 loss</p>
<p> Interest (receivable)  0.1		    vs 0.1</p>
<p> Tax			  0.8		    vs 1.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.5 loss	     vs 1.8 loss</p>
<p> Retained		   1.9 loss	     vs 2.1 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 14</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 22</p>
<p>NOTE - UK greeting cards company Clinton Cards Plc said that in the five weeks to September 8 turnover had increased by 30.3 percent and like-for-like sales rose by 11.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
